{"route":"/docs/5.1/content/typography/","version":"5.1","renderedVersion":"5.1","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Typography","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Documentation and examples for Bootstrap typography, including global settings, headings, body text, lists, and more."},"blocks":[{"id":"global-settings","type":"heading","en":"Global settings","level":2},{"id":"global-settings--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Bootstrap sets basic global display, typography, and link styles. When more control is needed, check out the <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/utilities/text/\">textual utility classes</a>."},{"id":"global-settings--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"global-settings--item-1","type":"item","en":"Use a <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/content/reboot/#native-font-stack\">native font stack</a> that selects the best <code>font-family</code> for each OS and device."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"global-settings--item-2","type":"item","en":"For a more inclusive and accessible type scale, we use the browser’s default root <code>font-size</code> (typically 16px) so visitors can customize their browser defaults as needed."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"global-settings--item-3","type":"item","en":"Use the <code>$font-family-base</code>, <code>$font-size-base</code>, and <code>$line-height-base</code> attributes as our typographic base applied to the <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"global-settings--item-4","type":"item","en":"Set the global link color via <code>$link-color</code>."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"global-settings--item-5","type":"item","en":"Use <code>$body-bg</code> to set a <code>background-color</code> on the <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> (<code>#fff</code> by default)."}]}]},{"id":"global-settings--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"These styles can be found within <code>_reboot.scss</code>, and the global variables are defined in <code>_variables.scss</code>. Make sure to set <code>$font-size-base</code> in <code>rem</code>."},{"id":"headings","type":"heading","en":"Headings","level":2},{"id":"headings--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"All HTML headings, <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> through <code>&lt;h6&gt;</code>, are available."},{"id":"headings--table-1","type":"table","caption":[],"rows":[{"head":true,"cells":[{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Heading"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Example"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>&lt;h1&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"h1. Bootstrap heading"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-6","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>&lt;h2&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-7","type":"paragraph","en":"h2. Bootstrap heading"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-8","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>&lt;h3&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-9","type":"paragraph","en":"h3. Bootstrap heading"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-10","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>&lt;h4&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-11","type":"paragraph","en":"h4. Bootstrap heading"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-12","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>&lt;h5&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-13","type":"paragraph","en":"h5. Bootstrap heading"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-14","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>&lt;h6&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"headings--paragraph-15","type":"paragraph","en":"h6. Bootstrap heading"}]}]}]},{"id":"headings--code-1","type":"code","value":"<h1>h1. Bootstrap heading</h1>\n<h2>h2. Bootstrap heading</h2>\n<h3>h3. Bootstrap heading</h3>\n<h4>h4. Bootstrap heading</h4>\n<h5>h5. Bootstrap heading</h5>\n<h6>h6. Bootstrap heading</h6>","language":"html"},{"id":"headings--paragraph-16","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>.h1</code> through <code>.h6</code> classes are also available, for when you want to match the font styling of a heading but cannot use the associated HTML element."},{"id":"headings--example-1","type":"demo","key":"cf8164e46bd5254a5ff7","height":300},{"id":"headings--code-2","type":"code","value":"<p class=\"h1\">h1. Bootstrap heading</p>\n<p class=\"h2\">h2. Bootstrap heading</p>\n<p class=\"h3\">h3. Bootstrap heading</p>\n<p class=\"h4\">h4. Bootstrap heading</p>\n<p class=\"h5\">h5. Bootstrap heading</p>\n<p class=\"h6\">h6. Bootstrap heading</p>","language":"html"},{"id":"customizing-headings","type":"heading","en":"Customizing headings","level":3},{"id":"customizing-headings--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Use the included utility classes to recreate the small secondary heading text from Bootstrap 3."},{"id":"customizing-headings--example-1","type":"demo","key":"f29b68e4765122190240","height":147},{"id":"customizing-headings--code-1","type":"code","value":"<h3>\n  Fancy display heading\n  <small class=\"text-muted\">With faded secondary text</small>\n</h3>","language":"html"},{"id":"display-headings","type":"heading","en":"Display headings","level":2},{"id":"display-headings--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Traditional heading elements are designed to work best in the meat of your page content. When you need a heading to stand out, consider using a <strong>display heading</strong>—a larger, slightly more opinionated heading style."},{"id":"display-headings--example-1","type":"demo","key":"93c715f2eeb532306953","height":300},{"id":"display-headings--code-1","type":"code","value":"<h1 class=\"display-1\">Display 1</h1>\n<h1 class=\"display-2\">Display 2</h1>\n<h1 class=\"display-3\">Display 3</h1>\n<h1 class=\"display-4\">Display 4</h1>\n<h1 class=\"display-5\">Display 5</h1>\n<h1 class=\"display-6\">Display 6</h1>","language":"html"},{"id":"display-headings--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Display headings are configured via the <code>$display-font-sizes</code> Sass map and two variables, <code>$display-font-weight</code> and <code>$display-line-height</code>."},{"id":"display-headings--code-2","type":"code","value":"$display-font-sizes: (\n  1: 5rem,\n  2: 4.5rem,\n  3: 4rem,\n  4: 3.5rem,\n  5: 3rem,\n  6: 2.5rem\n);\n\n$display-font-weight: 300;\n$display-line-height: $headings-line-height;","language":"scss"},{"id":"lead","type":"heading","en":"Lead","level":2},{"id":"lead--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Make a paragraph stand out by adding <code>.lead</code>."},{"id":"lead--example-1","type":"demo","key":"16b8728fbc3cc329d84e","height":147},{"id":"lead--code-1","type":"code","value":"<p class=\"lead\">\n  This is a lead paragraph. It stands out from regular paragraphs.\n</p>","language":"html"},{"id":"inline-text-elements","type":"heading","en":"Inline text elements","level":2},{"id":"inline-text-elements--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Styling for common inline HTML5 elements."},{"id":"inline-text-elements--example-1","type":"demo","key":"762e9acb1ca20288ad5f","height":300},{"id":"inline-text-elements--code-1","type":"code","value":"<p>You can use the mark tag to <mark>highlight</mark> text.</p>\n<p><del>This line of text is meant to be treated as deleted text.</del></p>\n<p><s>This line of text is meant to be treated as no longer accurate.</s></p>\n<p><ins>This line of text is meant to be treated as an addition to the document.</ins></p>\n<p><u>This line of text will render as underlined.</u></p>\n<p><small>This line of text is meant to be treated as fine print.</small></p>\n<p><strong>This line rendered as bold text.</strong></p>\n<p><em>This line rendered as italicized text.</em></p>","language":"html"},{"id":"inline-text-elements--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Beware that those tags should be used for semantic purpose:"},{"id":"inline-text-elements--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"inline-text-elements--item-1","type":"item","en":"<code>&lt;mark&gt;</code> represents text which is marked or highlighted for reference or notation purposes."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"inline-text-elements--item-2","type":"item","en":"<code>&lt;small&gt;</code> represents side-comments and small print, like copyright and legal text."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"inline-text-elements--item-3","type":"item","en":"<code>&lt;s&gt;</code> represents element that are no longer relevant or no longer accurate."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"inline-text-elements--item-4","type":"item","en":"<code>&lt;u&gt;</code> represents a span of inline text which should be rendered in a way that indicates that it has a non-textual annotation."}]}]},{"id":"inline-text-elements--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"If you want to style your text, you should use the following classes instead:"},{"id":"inline-text-elements--list-2","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"inline-text-elements--item-5","type":"item","en":"<code>.mark</code> will apply the same styles as <code>&lt;mark&gt;</code>."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"inline-text-elements--item-6","type":"item","en":"<code>.small</code> will apply the same styles as <code>&lt;small&gt;</code>."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"inline-text-elements--item-7","type":"item","en":"<code>.text-decoration-underline</code> will apply the same styles as <code>&lt;u&gt;</code>."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"inline-text-elements--item-8","type":"item","en":"<code>.text-decoration-line-through</code> will apply the same styles as <code>&lt;s&gt;</code>."}]}]},{"id":"inline-text-elements--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"While not shown above, feel free to use <code>&lt;b&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;i&gt;</code> in HTML5. <code>&lt;b&gt;</code> is meant to highlight words or phrases without conveying additional importance, while <code>&lt;i&gt;</code> is mostly for voice, technical terms, etc."},{"id":"text-utilities","type":"heading","en":"Text utilities","level":2},{"id":"text-utilities--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Change text alignment, transform, style, weight, line-height, decoration and color with our <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/utilities/text/\">text utilities</a> and <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/utilities/colors/\">color utilities</a>."},{"id":"abbreviations","type":"heading","en":"Abbreviations","level":2},{"id":"abbreviations--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Stylized implementation of HTML’s <code>&lt;abbr&gt;</code> element for abbreviations and acronyms to show the expanded version on hover. Abbreviations have a default underline and gain a help cursor to provide additional context on hover and to users of assistive technologies."},{"id":"abbreviations--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Add <code>.initialism</code> to an abbreviation for a slightly smaller font-size."},{"id":"abbreviations--example-1","type":"demo","key":"ab48788b1b20051dede3","height":174},{"id":"abbreviations--code-1","type":"code","value":"<p><abbr title=\"attribute\">attr</abbr></p>\n<p><abbr title=\"HyperText Markup Language\" class=\"initialism\">HTML</abbr></p>","language":"html"},{"id":"blockquotes","type":"heading","en":"Blockquotes","level":2},{"id":"blockquotes--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"For quoting blocks of content from another source within your document. Wrap <code>&lt;blockquote class=&quot;blockquote&quot;&gt;</code> around any <abbr title=\"HyperText Markup Language\">HTML</abbr> as the quote."},{"id":"blockquotes--example-1","type":"demo","key":"7d67037dfca797b84cec","height":147},{"id":"blockquotes--code-1","type":"code","value":"<blockquote class=\"blockquote\">\n  <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n</blockquote>","language":"html"},{"id":"naming-a-source","type":"heading","en":"Naming a source","level":3},{"id":"naming-a-source--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"The HTML spec requires that blockquote attribution be placed outside the <code>&lt;blockquote&gt;</code>. When providing attribution, wrap your <code>&lt;blockquote&gt;</code> in a <code>&lt;figure&gt;</code> and use a <code>&lt;figcaption&gt;</code> or a block level element (e.g., <code>&lt;p&gt;</code>) with the <code>.blockquote-footer</code> class. Be sure to wrap the name of the source work in <code>&lt;cite&gt;</code> as well."},{"id":"naming-a-source--example-1","type":"demo","key":"f81bc32546050f5fc172","height":147},{"id":"naming-a-source--code-1","type":"code","value":"<figure>\n  <blockquote class=\"blockquote\">\n    <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n  </blockquote>\n  <figcaption class=\"blockquote-footer\">\n    Someone famous in <cite title=\"Source Title\">Source Title</cite>\n  </figcaption>\n</figure>","language":"html"},{"id":"alignment","type":"heading","en":"Alignment","level":3},{"id":"alignment--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Use text utilities as needed to change the alignment of your blockquote."},{"id":"alignment--example-1","type":"demo","key":"3a095e502e4bf75df87b","height":147},{"id":"alignment--code-1","type":"code","value":"<figure class=\"text-center\">\n  <blockquote class=\"blockquote\">\n    <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n  </blockquote>\n  <figcaption class=\"blockquote-footer\">\n    Someone famous in <cite title=\"Source Title\">Source Title</cite>\n  </figcaption>\n</figure>","language":"html"},{"id":"alignment--example-2","type":"demo","key":"68c634b6f658eca8fa7a","height":147},{"id":"alignment--code-2","type":"code","value":"<figure class=\"text-end\">\n  <blockquote class=\"blockquote\">\n    <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n  </blockquote>\n  <figcaption class=\"blockquote-footer\">\n    Someone famous in <cite title=\"Source Title\">Source Title</cite>\n  </figcaption>\n</figure>","language":"html"},{"id":"lists","type":"heading","en":"Lists","level":2},{"id":"unstyled","type":"heading","en":"Unstyled","level":3},{"id":"unstyled--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Remove the default <code>list-style</code> and left margin on list items (immediate children only). <strong>This only applies to immediate children list items</strong>, meaning you will need to add the class for any nested lists as well."},{"id":"unstyled--example-1","type":"demo","key":"da6c566bf76485ce6208","height":147},{"id":"unstyled--code-1","type":"code","value":"<ul class=\"list-unstyled\">\n  <li>This is a list.</li>\n  <li>It appears completely unstyled.</li>\n  <li>Structurally, it's still a list.</li>\n  <li>However, this style only applies to immediate child elements.</li>\n  <li>Nested lists:\n    <ul>\n      <li>are unaffected by this style</li>\n      <li>will still show a bullet</li>\n      <li>and have appropriate left margin</li>\n    </ul>\n  </li>\n  <li>This may still come in handy in some situations.</li>\n</ul>","language":"html"},{"id":"inline","type":"heading","en":"Inline","level":3},{"id":"inline--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Remove a list’s bullets and apply some light <code>margin</code> with a combination of two classes, <code>.list-inline</code> and <code>.list-inline-item</code>."},{"id":"inline--example-1","type":"demo","key":"3cb477196355488cca76","height":147},{"id":"inline--code-1","type":"code","value":"<ul class=\"list-inline\">\n  <li class=\"list-inline-item\">This is a list item.</li>\n  <li class=\"list-inline-item\">And another one.</li>\n  <li class=\"list-inline-item\">But they're displayed inline.</li>\n</ul>","language":"html"},{"id":"description-list-alignment","type":"heading","en":"Description list alignment","level":3},{"id":"description-list-alignment--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Align terms and descriptions horizontally by using our grid system’s predefined classes (or semantic mixins). For longer terms, you can optionally add a <code>.text-truncate</code> class to truncate the text with an ellipsis."},{"id":"description-list-alignment--example-1","type":"demo","key":"3f0a07b6fa54f50c89ff","height":147},{"id":"description-list-alignment--code-1","type":"code","value":"<dl class=\"row\">\n  <dt class=\"col-sm-3\">Description lists</dt>\n  <dd class=\"col-sm-9\">A description list is perfect for defining terms.</dd>\n\n  <dt class=\"col-sm-3\">Term</dt>\n  <dd class=\"col-sm-9\">\n    <p>Definition for the term.</p>\n    <p>And some more placeholder definition text.</p>\n  </dd>\n\n  <dt class=\"col-sm-3\">Another term</dt>\n  <dd class=\"col-sm-9\">This definition is short, so no extra paragraphs or anything.</dd>\n\n  <dt class=\"col-sm-3 text-truncate\">Truncated term is truncated</dt>\n  <dd class=\"col-sm-9\">This can be useful when space is tight. Adds an ellipsis at the end.</dd>\n\n  <dt class=\"col-sm-3\">Nesting</dt>\n  <dd class=\"col-sm-9\">\n    <dl class=\"row\">\n      <dt class=\"col-sm-4\">Nested definition list</dt>\n      <dd class=\"col-sm-8\">I heard you like definition lists. Let me put a definition list inside your definition list.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </dd>\n</dl>","language":"html"},{"id":"responsive-font-sizes","type":"heading","en":"Responsive font sizes","level":2},{"id":"responsive-font-sizes--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"In Bootstrap 5, we’ve enabled responsive font sizes by default, allowing text to scale more naturally across device and viewport sizes. Have a look at the <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/getting-started/rfs/\">RFS page</a> to find out how this works."},{"id":"sass","type":"heading","en":"Sass","level":2},{"id":"variables","type":"heading","en":"Variables","level":3},{"id":"variables--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Headings have some dedicated variables for sizing and spacing."},{"id":"variables--code-1","type":"code","value":"$headings-margin-bottom:      $spacer * .5;\n$headings-font-family:        null;\n$headings-font-style:         null;\n$headings-font-weight:        500;\n$headings-line-height:        1.2;\n$headings-color:              null;","language":"scss"},{"id":"variables--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Miscellaneous typography elements covered here and in <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/content/reboot/\">Reboot</a> also have dedicated variables."},{"id":"variables--code-2","type":"code","value":"$lead-font-size:              $font-size-base * 1.25;\n$lead-font-weight:            300;\n\n$small-font-size:             .875em;\n\n$sub-sup-font-size:           .75em;\n\n$text-muted:                  $gray-600;\n\n$initialism-font-size:        $small-font-size;\n\n$blockquote-margin-y:         $spacer;\n$blockquote-font-size:        $font-size-base * 1.25;\n$blockquote-footer-color:     $gray-600;\n$blockquote-footer-font-size: $small-font-size;\n\n$hr-margin-y:                 $spacer;\n$hr-color:                    inherit;\n$hr-height:                   $border-width;\n$hr-opacity:                  .25;\n\n$legend-margin-bottom:        .5rem;\n$legend-font-size:            1.5rem;\n$legend-font-weight:          null;\n\n$mark-padding:                .2em;\n\n$dt-font-weight:              $font-weight-bold;\n\n$nested-kbd-font-weight:      $font-weight-bold;\n\n$list-inline-padding:         .5rem;\n\n$mark-bg:                     #fcf8e3;","language":"scss"},{"id":"mixins","type":"heading","en":"Mixins","level":3},{"id":"mixins--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"There are no dedicated mixins for typography, but Bootstrap does use <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/getting-started/rfs/\">Responsive Font Sizing (RFS)</a>."}],"demos":[{"key":"cf8164e46bd5254a5ff7","html":"\n<p class=\"h1\">h1. Bootstrap heading</p>\n<p class=\"h2\">h2. Bootstrap heading</p>\n<p class=\"h3\">h3. Bootstrap heading</p>\n<p class=\"h4\">h4. Bootstrap heading</p>\n<p class=\"h5\">h5. Bootstrap heading</p>\n<p class=\"h6\">h6. Bootstrap heading</p>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"f29b68e4765122190240","html":"\n<h3>\n  Fancy display heading\n  <small class=\"text-muted\">With faded secondary text</small>\n</h3>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"93c715f2eeb532306953","html":"\n  <div class=\"display-1 pb-3 mb-3 border-bottom\">Display 1</div>\n  <div class=\"display-2 pb-3 mb-3 border-bottom\">Display 2</div>\n  <div class=\"display-3 pb-3 mb-3 border-bottom\">Display 3</div>\n  <div class=\"display-4 pb-3 mb-3 border-bottom\">Display 4</div>\n  <div class=\"display-5 pb-3 mb-3 border-bottom\">Display 5</div>\n  <div class=\"display-6\">Display 6</div>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"16b8728fbc3cc329d84e","html":"\n<p class=\"lead\">\n  This is a lead paragraph. It stands out from regular paragraphs.\n</p>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"762e9acb1ca20288ad5f","html":"\n<p>You can use the mark tag to <mark>highlight</mark> text.</p>\n<p><del>This line of text is meant to be treated as deleted text.</del></p>\n<p><s>This line of text is meant to be treated as no longer accurate.</s></p>\n<p><ins>This line of text is meant to be treated as an addition to the document.</ins></p>\n<p><u>This line of text will render as underlined.</u></p>\n<p><small>This line of text is meant to be treated as fine print.</small></p>\n<p><strong>This line rendered as bold text.</strong></p>\n<p><em>This line rendered as italicized text.</em></p>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"ab48788b1b20051dede3","html":"\n<p><abbr title=\"attribute\">attr</abbr></p>\n<p><abbr title=\"HyperText Markup Language\" class=\"initialism\">HTML</abbr></p>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"7d67037dfca797b84cec","html":"\n<blockquote class=\"blockquote\">\n  <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n</blockquote>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"f81bc32546050f5fc172","html":"\n<figure>\n  <blockquote class=\"blockquote\">\n    <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n  </blockquote>\n  <figcaption class=\"blockquote-footer\">\n    Someone famous in <cite title=\"Source Title\">Source Title</cite>\n  </figcaption>\n</figure>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"3a095e502e4bf75df87b","html":"\n<figure class=\"text-center\">\n  <blockquote class=\"blockquote\">\n    <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n  </blockquote>\n  <figcaption class=\"blockquote-footer\">\n    Someone famous in <cite title=\"Source Title\">Source Title</cite>\n  </figcaption>\n</figure>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"68c634b6f658eca8fa7a","html":"\n<figure class=\"text-end\">\n  <blockquote class=\"blockquote\">\n    <p>A well-known quote, contained in a blockquote element.</p>\n  </blockquote>\n  <figcaption class=\"blockquote-footer\">\n    Someone famous in <cite title=\"Source Title\">Source Title</cite>\n  </figcaption>\n</figure>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"da6c566bf76485ce6208","html":"\n<ul class=\"list-unstyled\">\n  <li>This is a list.</li>\n  <li>It appears completely unstyled.</li>\n  <li>Structurally, it's still a list.</li>\n  <li>However, this style only applies to immediate child elements.</li>\n  <li>Nested lists:\n    <ul>\n      <li>are unaffected by this style</li>\n      <li>will still show a bullet</li>\n      <li>and have appropriate left margin</li>\n    </ul>\n  </li>\n  <li>This may still come in handy in some situations.</li>\n</ul>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"3cb477196355488cca76","html":"\n<ul class=\"list-inline\">\n  <li class=\"list-inline-item\">This is a list item.</li>\n  <li class=\"list-inline-item\">And another one.</li>\n  <li class=\"list-inline-item\">But they're displayed inline.</li>\n</ul>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"3f0a07b6fa54f50c89ff","html":"\n<dl class=\"row\">\n  <dt class=\"col-sm-3\">Description lists</dt>\n  <dd class=\"col-sm-9\">A description list is perfect for defining terms.</dd>\n\n  <dt class=\"col-sm-3\">Term</dt>\n  <dd class=\"col-sm-9\">\n    <p>Definition for the term.</p>\n    <p>And some more placeholder definition text.</p>\n  </dd>\n\n  <dt class=\"col-sm-3\">Another term</dt>\n  <dd class=\"col-sm-9\">This definition is short, so no extra paragraphs or anything.</dd>\n\n  <dt class=\"col-sm-3 text-truncate\">Truncated term is truncated</dt>\n  <dd class=\"col-sm-9\">This can be useful when space is tight. Adds an ellipsis at the end.</dd>\n\n  <dt class=\"col-sm-3\">Nesting</dt>\n  <dd class=\"col-sm-9\">\n    <dl class=\"row\">\n      <dt class=\"col-sm-4\">Nested definition list</dt>\n      <dd class=\"col-sm-8\">I heard you like definition lists. Let me put a definition list inside your definition list.</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </dd>\n</dl>\n","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""}],"nav":[{"en":"Introduction","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/getting-started/introduction/"},{"en":"Download","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/getting-started/download/"},{"en":"Contents","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/getting-started/contents/"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/getting-started/browsers-devices/"},{"en":"JavaScript","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/getting-started/javascript/"},{"en":"Webpack","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/getting-started/webpack/"},{"en":"Parcel","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/getting-started/parcel/"},{"en":"Accessibility","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.1/getting-started/accessibility/"},{"en":"RFS","href":"https://getbootstrap.com